<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ============================================================
    ic_muted_small — chat-list "muted conversation" indicator
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    Referenced by item_conversation.xml's iv_muted, in the
    top-right metadata cluster (next to the pin and timestamp).

    Constraints this file honors:

    1. MONOCHROME. Both <path> elements fill with #FFFFFFFF.
       The consuming ImageView applies
       app:tint="?attr/colorOnSurfaceVariant" at layout time,
       which is what determines the actual rendered color (a
       low-emphasis gray in both light and dark themes). Do NOT
       set a colored fill here — it would be tinted away by the
       ImageView's app:tint, so the fill value would have zero
       effect but would mislead future maintainers into thinking
       the file has a color.

    2. 14dp VIEWPORT, matching ic_pin_small.xml exactly. Both
       indicators render side-by-side in the same metadata
       cluster; if one were 12dp or 16dp, they would visually
       clash. Any future change to the metadata cluster's icon
       size must update BOTH files simultaneously.

    3. "CUT-THROUGH" SLASH, not a stripe ON TOP. The bell is
       a solid silhouette and the slash is a HOLE in it, not a
       line drawn over it. This is achieved with two contours
       in the SAME <path> element, using fillType="evenOdd":

         - Outer contour: bell silhouette
         - Inner contour: the slash rectangle

       With evenOdd, a point inside both contours has crossing
       number 2 (even) → NOT filled (the hole). A point inside
       only the slash (i.e., the parts of the slash that extend
       beyond the bell) has crossing number 1 → filled. The
       result is a bell shape with a clean diagonal cut through
       it, plus visible diagonal lines where the slash extends
       beyond the bell's edges.

       If you were to switch to fillType="nonZero" (or remove
       fillType entirely), the slash contour would fill IN
       ADDITION to the bell, and the visible result would be a
       normal notification bell with an extra diagonal line
       sitting on top of it — which reads as "bell with a
       stripe" not "bell with a slash." Do NOT change the
       fillType.

    4. CLAPPER as a SEPARATE <path>. The little rounded nub
       below the bell body is a second <path> with default
       nonZero fill. It sits below the bell base with a small
       gap; both shapes are independent. This avoids one subtle
       problem: if the clapper were part of the same evenOdd
       path, its interior would have crossing number 2 whenever
       it overlapped the bell base by even a fraction of a unit,
       creating a 1-pixel hole at the top of the clapper on
       some GPU implementations. Keeping it separate and using
       nonZero avoids that class of artifact entirely.

    Do NOT reuse this icon at a different size. The clapper's
    gap and the slash's width have both been tuned for 14dp.
    At 24dp, the slash would look thin relative to the bell;
    at 18dp it would feel cramped. If a larger mute icon is
    ever needed (e.g., in a settings row), create a new
    ic_muted.xml at 24dp with recalibrated proportions rather
    than scaling this one.
    ============================================================
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="14dp"
    android:height="14dp"
    android:viewportWidth="14"
    android:viewportHeight="14">

    <!--
        ============================================================
        Path 1 — bell body + diagonal slash (as hole via evenOdd)
        ============================================================

        Bell outer contour:
            M 7,1.5                          → top-center of dome
            C 5.9,1.5 5,2.4 5,3.5            → curve into left
                                               shoulder (control
                                               points (5.9,1.5)
                                               and (5,2.4))
            V 3.8                            → tiny step down
            C 3.2,4.3 2,6 2,8                → curve out to the
                                               left side and
                                               down to (2,8)
            V 9.5                            → straight down
            L 1,10.5                         → flare out-left
            V 11.5                           → down to base
            H 13                             → flat base
            V 10.5                           → up
            L 12,9.5                         → flare in-right
            V 8                              → up
            C 12,6 10.8,4.3 9,3.8            → curve up-right
            V 3.5                            → tiny step up
            C 9,2.4 8.1,1.5 7,1.5            → curve back to
                                               top-center
            Z                                → close

        Slash inner contour (uses evenOdd to cut through bell):
            M 12.5,1    → top-right end, outside bell
            L 2.5,12    → bottom-left end, same side
            L 1.5,13    → bottom-left end, opposite side
            L 11.5,2    → top-right end, opposite side
            Z           → close

        With evenOdd, the intersection region (slash inside
        bell) is a hole; the parts of the slash outside the
        bell are filled as thin diagonal lines. That produces
        the classic "notifications off" look.
        ============================================================
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M7,1.5C5.9,1.5 5,2.4 5,3.5V3.8C3.2,4.3 2,6 2,8V9.5L1,10.5V11.5H13V10.5L12,9.5V8C12,6 10.8,4.3 9,3.8V3.5C9,2.4 8.1,1.5 7,1.5ZM12.5,1L2.5,12L1.5,13L11.5,2Z" />

    <!--
        ============================================================
        Path 2 — clapper (nub below the bell base)
        ============================================================

        M 7,13.5                             → bottom-center
        C 6.1,13.5 5.4,12.8 5.4,11.9        → curve up-left
        H 8.6                                → top edge
        C 8.6,12.8 7.9,13.5 7,13.5          → curve back to
                                               bottom-center
        Z

        Default fillType (nonZero) is intentional for this path
        — see the file comment above. This is a self-contained
        shape with no overlapping contours, so nonZero treats it
        as filled, which is what we want.
        ============================================================
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M7,13.5C6.1,13.5 5.4,12.8 5.4,11.9H8.6C8.6,12.8 7.9,13.5 7,13.5Z" />

</vector>
